  "llm_reasoning_text": "Q1: Indexes on date filter, store_sales FKs, demographics, and address state accelerate multi-condition joins.\n\nQ2: Indexes on catalog_sales FKs, item category, customer birth month, and address state speed up joins and filters.\n\nQ3: Indexes on date, store_sales FKs, item category, and customer address enable efficient join and filter execution.\n\nQ4: Three-way join between store_sales, store_returns, catalog_sales benefits from indexes on all join and date keys.\n\nQ5: Indexes on demographics filter columns, item category, store state, and date support efficient join traversal.\n\nQ6: Indexes on catalog_sales date and warehouse keys, plus item category and manager, speed up the date-range join.\n\nQ7: Indexes on date, store_returns ticket/item join keys, and store state filter accelerate the sales-returns join.\n\nQ8: Indexes on inventory item/date, catalog_sales FKs, week_seq, demographics, and item category improve this complex join.\n\nQ9: Indexes on customer FK columns, address city, income band bounds, and store_returns cdemo accelerate lookup joins.\n\nQ10: Indexes on web_returns FK columns and customer_demographics filter columns speed up the dual-cdemo join pattern.\n\nQ11: Indexes on catalog_returns date/customer/call_center keys and demographics filter columns accelerate the join chain.\n\nQ12: Indexes on catalog_sales ship date and all FK columns enable fast lookup of the date-range and dimension joins.\n\nQ13: Self-join on store_sales via ticket number benefits from indexes on item, customer, demographics, and date keys.\n\nQ14: Three-channel join (store/web/returns) benefits from indexes on all customer, item, date, and demographic FK columns.\n\nQ15: Complex multi-table join requires indexes on inventory, web/store sales FKs, item filters, and customer dimension keys.\n\nQ16: Indexes on date filter, store_sales FK columns, demographics, and address state speed up multi-condition joins.\n\nQ17: Indexes on catalog_sales FKs, date year, item category, and customer filters accelerate joins and filtering.\n\nQ18: Indexes on date year/month, item category, customer birth month, and address state accelerate join and filter operations.\n\nQ19: Indexes on ticket/item join keys and date columns speed up three-way sales/returns/catalog join with date filters.\n\nQ20: Indexes on date year, item category, demographics filter, and store_sales FK columns reduce scan and join cost.\n\nQ21: Indexes on catalog_sales date/item/warehouse and item category+manager speed up the left join and date range filter.\n\nQ22: Indexes on ticket/item composite keys and date dimensions accelerate the store_sales to store_returns join.\n\nQ23: Indexes on catalog_sales FKs, inventory composite, item category, and demographics filter support this multi-join query.\n\nQ24: Indexes on customer FK columns, address city, and income band bounds accelerate the multi-table customer lookup.\n\nQ25: Indexes on web_sales/returns join keys, demographics, and address state/country accelerate the complex web returns query.\n\nQ26: Indexes on catalog_returns date/call_center/customer and demographic filters speed up the call center returns analysis.\n\nQ27: Indexes on catalog_sales ship date and FK columns for warehouse, ship mode, and call center speed up shipping analysis.\n\nQ28: Indexes on store_sales ticket/item self-join keys, item category, and demographic filters support the item pair basket analysis.\n\nQ29: Indexes on cross-channel ticket/item keys, date, item category, and household income band support cross-channel customer analysis.\n\nQ30: Indexes on multi-channel item/customer/warehouse joins, inventory composite, item filters, and address state reduce cross-channel scan cost.\n\nQ31: Indexes accelerate the date join, store_returns grouping, and customer/demographics filtering by year, state, and attributes.\n\nQ32: Supports EXISTS subquery joins on customer_sk and date filtering, plus county and demographics lookups